1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Change history? Oh boy.

2
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:08,700
Yes, I want you to prove whether or not it can be done.

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:17,660
I'm curious to know if this unsalvageable ruin, this tragedy devoid of all hope, could possibly be prevented if we tried.

4
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:24,660
So you think there might be a chance? I mean, I've always heard it said that history will correct itself, but...

5
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:29,820
Sure, but do the people who say that typically have the power to put their money where their mouth is?

6
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,140
Well, no, I guess not.

7
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:40,680
Doesn't matter how crowded this world may get. The only one around who can interfere with time is me. And don't you forget it.

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:49,320
A little pointer, though. Remember that whatever you see before you is real. And whatever moment you're in is the only truth there is, so be present.

9
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,900
Will I really be able to save Origami?

10
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,540
Hard to say. That really depends on you.

11
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,580
All right. I'm in. Let's do it.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,780
Would you care to explain what you're doing?

13
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,400
Cutting through this way will be a lot faster.

14
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:23,140
Who the heck are you?

15
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,240
Um, sorry. Gotta go!

16
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:27,380
Hey! You get back here!

17
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:29,440
Shido?

18
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:33,580
Shoot! I can't afford to waste time like this!

19
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:36,320
But now, what do I do?

20
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:42,380
Shido?

21
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,440
Yep, just me.

22
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,580
Have you seen anyone sketchy come through here?

23
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,760
Uh, no, I haven't seen anybody.

24
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:50,880
Really?

25
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:51,940
That's weird.

26
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,260
Is it?

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,380
Huh.

28
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,040
Oh, never mind. Don't you worry about it.

29
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,440
Tell your mom hi for me, okay?

30
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:03,200
Oh, that was a close one.

31
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,760
Good thinking. I'm impressed.

32
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:06,080
Yeah.

33
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:11,620
Never would have imagined that I'd used Natsumi's transformation powers, but they came in super handy.

34
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,360
I'll say they did.

35
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,600
Looking like that, no one will bat an eye seeing you in the past.

36
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,640
Yeah, sure. But how do I get back to normal?

37
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,060
Oh, you're so cute. Why would you bother?

38
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,400
Yeah, very funny.

39
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:32,700
That must be Coterie.

40
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,000
So it would seem.

41
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,320
Let's go!

42
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:52,340
A girl defies time and transforms into a devil, while a solitary boy goes up against an impending disaster.

43
00:02:54,060 --> 00:03:24,040
A girl defies time and transforms into a devil, while a solitary boy goes up against an impending disaster.

44
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,400
Oh, he says it.

45
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,020
A girl defies time and strumming la peatzie in the future.

46
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:30,380
Oh, he's my sister.

47
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:32,700
What does that make up against an impending disaster?

48
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:33,900
Oh, I don't caver.

49
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:34,840
I don't know.

50
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,140
It sucks.

51
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:42,140
Alright, let's go!

52
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,600
Let's revive what did you do here.

53
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,880
Keep it up and breathe back.

54
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:50,380
Send me what to the fresh air, okay?

55
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,820
I know it doesn't.

56
00:03:52,820 --> 00:04:22,800
I'll see you next time.

57
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:52,800
I'll see you next time.

58
00:04:52,820 --> 00:05:22,800
I'll see you next time.

59
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,000
She can't hear me!

60
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:26,140
Origami!

61
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,340
Come on!

62
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:28,720
Origami!

63
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,640
Mom and Dad, there you are.

64
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:46,440
Shido?

65
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,000
Don't worry, I'm fine.

66
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,640
But did they...

67
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,140
Wait.

68
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:52,600
No!

69
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:52,640
No!

70
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,420
You did this!

71
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:14,220
I'll never forgive you!

72
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,220
Never!

73
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,460
I'll kill you!

74
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:20,000
I swear I will!

75
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:24,460
Someday, I'll kill you!

76
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:27,460
I don't believe it.

77
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,300
What the hell's going on?

78
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,440
This is insane!

79
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:37,980
Not really.

80
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,360
For someone like Origami to have ended up in her current state,

81
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,380
I knew for a fact something significant had to have happened.

82
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:52,820
She's gone!

83
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:55,320
Yujbat must have reached its limit.

84
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:59,220
She went back to her original time.

85
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,420
No way.

86
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:06,420
So I guess this means Origami wasn't able to change history after all.

87
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,240
This is terrible.

88
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,780
Hey, Origami!

89
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:16,800
Watch out!

90
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:24,060
Sorry to knock you down.

91
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,660
Are you okay?

92
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,380
They're gone now.

93
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,120
They're both gone.

94
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,380
I don't...

95
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:36,380
Origami...

96
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:38,300
Sorry.

97
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,720
I'm so sorry.

98
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,520
Who are you?

99
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,000
It's all right.

100
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:45,880
It's gonna be all right.

101
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,280
Listen to me.

102
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,100
Someday you'll understand.

103
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:50,340
I promise.

104
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,480
All of this.

105
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:52,460
The truth.

106
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:54,620
But please don't forget.

107
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:56,880
You are never alone, okay?

108
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,020
I'm not.

109
00:07:59,400 --> 00:07:59,800
What?

110
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,560
All of your sadness and your hate!

111
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:03,640
Let me carry all of it for you!

112
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:05,940
If you're lost, I'll find you!

113
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:10,520
When something happens and it's too much, please come to me!

114
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:11,820
Give it all to me!

115
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,460
Everything!

116
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:13,200
It's okay!

117
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,520
I'll take all of it!

118
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:15,780
Do you hear me?

119
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:16,540
Okay?

120
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,480
Don't let despair take you over, Origami!

121
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:19,960
Thanks.

122
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:37,740
You're very kind.

123
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:38,020
Thanks.

124
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,140
You're very kind.

125
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:41,500
But who exactly are you anyway?

126
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:46,420
Uh, oh, I'm, uh, my name is Shido Itsuka.

127
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,720
I just live in the neighborhood.

128
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:50,800
Shido Itsuka.

129
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,720
Did you really mean everything you just said?

130
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,880
Yeah, of course. I meant every word.

131
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:56,960
Okay.

132
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:01,400
Well then, this will be the last time I ever cry.

133
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:06,380
But it's also the last time I'll smile.

134
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,060
What?

135
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:11,360
All my sadness and my joy, all the fun in my life.

136
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,700
I give to you.

137
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:16,260
But this anger, this anger is mine alone.

138
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:20,940
I'm going to kill that thing, that angel.

139
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:24,980
No matter what it takes, no matter how long it takes.

140
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,420
Origami, wait.

141
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:32,560
So sure, you can carry everything for me, till I'm ready to kill the angel.

142
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:34,500
Until then.

143
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:42,420
So that's what happened.

144
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:48,740
What an ironic turn of events.

145
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:56,220
How unexpected.

146
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,560
This is disappointing.

147
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,100
I'm sorry.

148
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:03,840
You used Yudbed, and I still couldn't do anything to fix this.

149
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,980
No, that's not what I'm talking about.

150
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:06,720
What?

151
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:10,640
Shida, we just learned Origami's the one who killed her parents.

152
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:15,100
And that means, this whole situation wouldn't have happened if not for my Zath-Kil.

153
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,640
So I have to be honest.

154
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,080
That's more than a little upsetting to me.

155
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,160
Hold on.

156
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:23,000
I think you're being a little unfair to yourself, don't you?

157
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:25,000
I mean, you didn't want this to happen.

158
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,320
No, of course not.

159
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,400
Anyway, it doesn't matter because it's all over now.

160
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:39,400
Is that really what you think?

161
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,200
It's true.

162
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,900
As far as that world is concerned, what's done is done.

163
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:44,740
Full stop.

164
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:50,240
However, I just happened to be presented with a new method to fix this mess only a moment ago.

165
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:52,540
What are you talking about presented?

166
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,380
By who?

167
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:56,680
Believe it or not, by you a few dozen minutes from now.

168
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,540
You mean the future, me?

169
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,000
I don't get it. Why would I do that?

170
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:07,860
Because the method future you told me about isn't one that the you who went to the past was aware of.

171
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,140
Do you understand?

172
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:14,760
You're saying that for this me right now, there's still a chance I can save Origami?

173
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,000
You got it.

174
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,280
Apparently this isn't over yet.

175
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:18,960
Let's go!

176
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:20,100
Indeed.

177
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:24,480
I agree, it's about time we went ahead and fixed this poor excuse for a world.

178
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:25,020
Yes.

179
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,940
I'll do literally anything to save her.

180
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:30,260
That a boy, that's the spirit.

181
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:33,040
So, how do we do that?

182
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,020
It's pretty simple in theory.

183
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:37,860
Basically, we're just going to have you try again.

184
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:38,620
Huh?

185
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:39,740
What do you mean?

186
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:44,240
If you think about it, what was the main reason you weren't able to stop Origami?

187
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,400
It was because you had no idea what was about to happen.

188
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:48,800
Do you see where I'm going?

189
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,720
Yeah, I think I get it now.

190
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:55,520
Well, the gist is that you're suggesting we use you'd bet on me again, is that right?

191
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:59,200
An interesting guess, for sure, but I'm afraid that's impossible.

192
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:03,000
As it stands now, I'm simply sharing your senses.

193
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:04,240
Or have you forgotten?

194
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,960
I can't physically interact with you in any way.

195
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,580
Then what?

196
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,180
There's another option.

197
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:13,520
One single method that only I know and can make happen.

198
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:22,180
Is this the right place?

199
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:23,480
Oh, absolutely.

200
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:24,900
Without a doubt.

201
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,420
I don't see anything.

202
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:29,220
Well, well, lucky me.

203
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:33,440
I will say, it's definitely not every day that a guest stumbles upon us out here.

204
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,180
Kurumi?

205
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:37,720
When you know my name right off the bat, that's another story.

206
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,280
Who are you?

207
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,100
And what the hell do you want?

208
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,700
You five years ago?

209
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:52,940
Yes.

210
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:56,600
It so happens I was also near the scene when this all occurred.

211
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,060
What the hell were you doing there?

212
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,700
Just checking out what was up with that blaze.

213
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:05,140
I had the sneaking suspicion that a spirit might be part of an inferno that size.

214
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:06,740
That makes sense.

215
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:09,820
So then what you want me to do is...

216
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:10,260
Yep.

217
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,540
You get to go ask me to shoot you.

218
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,040
With you'd bet.

219
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:16,780
Listen, I need your help.

220
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:19,820
You are not to move without my permission.

221
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,280
I can't guarantee you'll survive.

222
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,480
I'm Shido Itsuka.

223
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,840
I came from five years in the future.

224
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,820
And Kurumi, you're the one who sent me.

225
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:32,360
I swear, if this is some kind of joke...

226
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:33,640
This is not a joke!

227
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:34,220
Oh?

228
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:35,320
Listen!

229
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:37,200
Please, I need you to listen!

230
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,020
My goodness.

231
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:41,320
The old Mi sure was a cautious little thing, wasn't she?

232
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:43,160
Let's try something.

233
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:46,760
Shido, do you think you could have that Mi physically touch you?

234
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:47,680
I'll try.

235
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:50,040
Did you just mumble something?

236
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:51,420
Kurumi?

237
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,480
Would you come touch my hand?

238
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,020
You can keep the gun on me.

239
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,880
Future Kurumi wants to talk.

240
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:00,740
Wait, I said that?

241
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:08,380
Scale of one to ten.

242
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,980
How weird is it if I start with a long time no see?

243
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,200
Very interesting.

244
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:16,160
You definitely have my voice, so that's a good start.

245
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,380
Want to tell me what this is all about?

246
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:21,680
I see.

247
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:26,740
So you're saying all you want me to do is point Yudbet at him and shoot, is that right?

248
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:28,280
Yes.

249
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,500
I'd say that's precisely what I want.

250
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,460
Very well, then.

251
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:33,780
Really?

252
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:36,760
I can't very well refuse myself, can I?

253
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,580
Now, come to me!

254
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:41,720
Zafkiel!

255
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,800
It appears your time is now!

256
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:45,060
Zafkiel.

257
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:46,720
Yudbet.

258
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:50,140
All right.

259
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:51,380
Shall we proceed, then?

260
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,180
Yeah.

261
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:56,520
Orikami, this time it'll work.

262
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,060
I wish you the best of luck, stranger.

263
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,000
Shido.

264
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,600
Oh, Shido.

265
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:15,220
Looks like it must have worked.

266
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:18,340
All right, let's change the world.

267
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:22,200
Can I assume you have some sort of plan, then?

268
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:25,620
Tick tock.

269
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,980
Time's a-wastin'.

270
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:28,440
Look, stop pressuring me, okay?

271
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,460
I haven't really had time to think about it.

272
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:34,800
Remember, you and I both know exactly what's about to happen next.

273
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:40,160
So I vote you prevent Origami from realizing who killed her parents.

274
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,860
Sound like a good plan to you.

275
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:43,660
I considered that, too.

276
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:47,600
But it doesn't address the enormous problem that her parents will still die.

277
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,240
Hmm.

278
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,000
Let's be real.

279
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:58,880
As long as her parents are killed at the hand of a spirit, any spirit, she can end up directing that grudge towards anyone at all.

280
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:03,300
On Coterie, who caused the Inferno.

281
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:06,740
Or Phantom, the one who gave her the power to do that.

282
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:09,920
What's going on in that head, Shido?

283
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,840
Wouldn't it work out if...

284
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,600
If Origami appeared, but there was no enemy in sight?

285
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,660
Well, yeah, it's possible, but...

286
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:18,980
Good.

287
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:20,840
There's something I want to try.

288
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:28,540
Okay, you do realize you're creeping around like a pervert.

289
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:29,960
Shut up.

290
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:33,820
By the way, I assume you know this, but it never hurts to clarify.

291
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,320
You can't interact with Coterie or the others.

292
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,800
Yeah, I get that.

293
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:41,700
I shouldn't tamper with history any more than necessary.

294
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,600
The only thing I'm here to do is to save Origami.

295
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,480
Shido?

296
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:48,620
It's here.

297
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,520
Try to refrain, would you?

298
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:26,040
Coterie, I'm sorry.

299
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,400
Hey!

300
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,040
So you're Phantom.

301
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:32,960
Been waiting.

302
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,680
You're...

303
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,120
It can't be.

304
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:37,960
Why are you...

305
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,680
Wait a minute.

306
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,920
How do you know me?

307
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:42,900
Better hurry.

308
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:44,080
I'm on it.

309
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,660
Didn't see that reaction coming, did you?

310
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:51,480
Is that someone you're already acquainted with, Shido?

311
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:52,500
Nope.

312
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:55,100
Can't say I know anyone who censors their entire body.

313
00:17:55,100 --> 00:18:01,300
I have to admit, I never would have imagined that your big plan would basically consist of chatting with Phantom.

314
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,780
Is that a problem?

315
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:04,240
Of course not.

316
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:06,740
And it's so incredibly like you to attempt that.

317
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,680
But, I can't say it'd be my recommendation.

318
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:13,300
The fact is, that one is impossible to predict.

319
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,120
Do you know who she is then?

320
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,320
Phantom.

321
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,540
Huh, Phantom, is it?

322
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:23,240
Am I to understand that's the name I've been given?

323
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:27,200
I apologize for running off like that before.

324
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,880
I thought it would be better to do this away from her.

325
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,680
Oh, sorry.

326
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,340
Should have done this sooner.

327
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,120
Is that what you look like?

328
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:37,340
Well, no.

329
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,720
This isn't my real appearance.

330
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:42,380
I don't think I can show you what I actually look like just yet.

331
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:45,120
So, do you know who I am or something?

332
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,040
I do.

333
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,540
Very well, yes.

334
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:50,860
So?

335
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,940
Is that really all you wanted?

336
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:58,140
You went through the trouble of using a time travel bullet to come back here.

337
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,440
This isn't just a vacation, is it?

338
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,620
How do you know all this?

339
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:03,880
Fine.

340
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:05,420
I'll get straight to the point then.

341
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,820
I need you to disappear right now.

342
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:11,460
Is that your poetic way of saying that you're here to kill me?

343
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,880
No, this is about saving someone.

344
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,220
I just want you to get out of sight.

345
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:17,180
Fast.

346
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:18,280
I see.

347
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,440
Sorry, but my answer is no.

348
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:25,400
I'm afraid that I still have a few things I have to do.

349
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,320
Please, just go.

350
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,820
Origami is about to...

351
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:32,020
Shido, what's going on?

352
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:32,680
What's wrong?

353
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:37,700
Wait.

354
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,380
Why does this feel so familiar?

355
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:42,880
When the time is right, we should meet again.

356
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,120
I promise you.

357
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,700
This time I'll never let go.

358
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:51,140
I won't make that same mistake again.

359
00:19:51,140 --> 00:20:02,440
Are you okay, Shido?

360
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:03,400
Breathe.

361
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:04,980
Yeah, I'm fine.

362
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,760
Who the heck was she?

363
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:17,220
Don't tell me.

364
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:18,780
Origami!

365
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:23,420
Don't, Origami!

366
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:36,880
I won't let it.

367
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:36,900
I won't let it.

368
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:37,980
I can't let that happen to her again.

369
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:44,320
I will change the past!

370
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:47,460
Just hold on, okay?

371
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:48,900
I'm coming!

372
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:50,640
Origami!

373
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:55,180
Mom and Dad, there you are.

374
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:01,900
No Origami!

375
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:02,580
Doubt!

376
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:06,040
There's no use.

377
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,100
It's too late.

378
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:07,520
Dammit!

379
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:08,540
No, it's not!

380
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:09,240
Shido, wait!

381
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:24,840
I did it!

382
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:24,900
I did it!

383
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:44,500
What the...

384
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:49,220
Wait, wasn't I...

385
00:21:49,220 --> 00:21:49,960
Kurumi?

386
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:50,780
Kurumi!

387
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:53,720
Did it work?

388
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:54,920
Did I do it?

389
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:58,000
Was I able to save them?

390
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:01,000
Origami...

391
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,000
And her parents?

392
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:10,660
Let's make a promise to you and the last one.

393
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:24,940
No Origami!

394
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:31,160
傷だらけのままでしないこんでた心

395
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:36,360
君はそっと拾い上げた

396
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:43,300
繰り返す日々どうしようもなく紡いだとき

397
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:47,240
ぎゅっと抱き締めてくれた

398
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:54,240
I'm always here, you and two of them.

399
00:22:54,240 --> 00:23:01,240
I'll see you next time.

400
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:06,240
I'll see you next time.

401
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:12,240
I'll see you next time.

402
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:22,240
See you next time.

